Helm Security
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand Helm security best practices and common vulnerabilities
Manage Kubernetes Secrets securely using Helm
Implement security configurations (security contexts, RBAC, network policies) for Helm charts
Use Helm hooks and chart tests to validate secure deployment workflows
Audit deployed Helm releases against a security compliance checklist
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments, namespaces)
Familiarity with YAML syntax and Helm template syntax ({{ }}, range, with, if)
Basic knowledge of Linux command line operations
Understanding of container security concepts (non-root users, capabilities, read-only filesystems)
Previous experience with Helm basics (installation, charts, releases)
